    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1081">

                <pb facs="1044" n="1032" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg1032"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890E.00/213: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Egypt</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-11-15T13:00:00+02:00">November 15,
                            1943—1 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 16—8:54 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2095. My 2086, November 15, 1 p.m. In absence of King from Cairo I communicated
                    to him today through the First Chamberlain <pb facs="1045" n="1033"
                        xml:id="pg1033"/> the same information regarding the attitude of the
                    American Government on the Lebanese crisis which I conveyed to Nahas Pasha last
                    night.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
